On Tue, Mar 30, 2010 at 12:34 PM, Michael Everson
<michael.everson@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> So you're treating .i like a danda, or | not belonging to either sentence? What do people think about that?

Syntactically, it is clearly a separator. But notice that so are ".i
je", ".i ca bo", and such. It's not always just the single ".i" that
is the separator.

The tricky bit are the attitudinals that follow the separator, because
semantically they apply to the following sentence but syntactically
they attach to the separator.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

